Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Record where each claim in the shell contract came from

The review asked for provenance: which build this was checked against, and
what to grep to spot-check a claim without re-deriving it. Adds the desktop
version (0.0.203), the SHA-256 of each artifact read, and a table of the
literal behind every constant in the document; the bundle keeps its source
paths, so src/server/boot-phase.ts and src/server/services/orchestrator-lock.ts
are named as the places to look.

Also states the staleness risk plainly: no handshake carries a protocol
version, so a build that renames a phase or moves a budget breaks a client
silently. The shape is what to rely on; the constants are what to re-read per
release. And scopes the page away from the direction question in the companion
issue -- a harness or a diagnostics client needs these facts regardless.
